  "description": "Derived from the Arabic word “harir,” harira translates into “silk,” which describes the consistency of the soup. This version features both lentils and chickpeas, and is finished with a drizzle of beaten egg.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Cilantro leaves, for serving; Lemon wedges, for serving\n\nOptional substitutions: ghee → unsalted butter; lightly salted homemade vegetable stock → store-bought low-sodium vegetable broth\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The soup can be made and refrigerated for up to 5 days.",
